invariant: INV-17
file: gcm_avx512.c
catches: proof/prove-one.sh gcm_avx512_wipe
reason: wipe_frame's array holds half of GCM_AVX512_BELOW_LEN, so each
  entry wipes 1,280 bytes below its frame. The kernel's frames measured
  about 1,100 bytes deep at -O2, so the residue search after an entry may
  still find nothing, and the constant the Makefile reads for lint-stack's
  ceiling has not changed. The harness records the length ct_wipe runs
  and requires GCM_AVX512_BELOW_LEN.

--- old
    uint8_t below[GCM_AVX512_BELOW_LEN];
--- new
    uint8_t below[GCM_AVX512_BELOW_LEN / 2];
